course: dictionary
lesson: 7502
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Potassium is one of these words. Look at the clues around it before you decide.
explain: «Farmers add nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium to soil as fertiliser to grow more food.» Here potassium is a chemical that helps plants grow. The clues are soil, fertiliser and grow more food.
explain: «Bananas contain potassium, but most exercise cramp is thought to come from tired muscles.» Here potassium is a mineral in food that your body needs. The clues are bananas, contain and muscles. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Potassium is a soft, silvery metal with the symbol K.
fact: Potassium is also a mineral your body needs to keep the heart, muscles and nerves working.
fact: Foods rich in potassium include bananas, potatoes and beans.
fact: Potassium reacts very strongly with water, so teachers keep it under oil and only they handle it.
fact: «Potassium chloride» is the name of a chemical that contains potassium.
exercise: «Farmers add nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium to soil as fertiliser to grow more food.» In this sentence, what is potassium? | A plant that grows in the soil | A type of cloud | A kind of farm animal | *A chemical that helps plants grow
exercise: Tom yells for a banana to stop his cramp. Which food is famous for containing potassium? | Cheese | *Bananas | Bread
exercise: Why is potassium kept under oil in a science lab? | It tastes nice to the teacher | It needs to stay cold like ice | *It reacts strongly with water | It keeps the metal shiny for the class
test: Potassium is a soft, silvery ___ with the symbol K. | plastic | *metal | cloud
test: Which mineral does the body need to keep the heart, muscles and nerves working? | Sugar | *Potassium | Plastic
exam: Scientists think most exercise cramp comes from what? | Eating too many bananas | Wearing the wrong socks | *Tired muscles
